WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.079 --> 00:00:05.790
Bradley Cooper and Lady Gaga join forces to
give us a new take on the classic love story

00:00:05.790 --> 00:00:10.380
A Star Is Born, which follows a struggling
young artist and a veteran performer battling

00:00:10.380 --> 00:00:11.380
addiction.

00:00:11.380 --> 00:00:14.990
Yippee-ki-yay, movie lovers, it's Jan here,
and in this video I'm going to reveal ten

00:00:14.990 --> 00:00:18.760
behind-the-scenes secrets and fascinating
facts about the making of the new A Star Is

00:00:18.760 --> 00:00:19.910
Born movie.

00:00:19.910 --> 00:00:23.500
Make sure you keep watching to the end to
find out the heart-breaking real-life story

00:00:23.500 --> 00:00:26.310
behind Lady Gaga's final song [in the film].

00:00:26.310 --> 00:00:30.410
The first time Ally and Jackson meet, she's
performing in a drag bar, belting out Édith

00:00:30.410 --> 00:00:32.960
Piaf's classic love song La Vie en Rose.

00:00:32.960 --> 00:00:36.589
And, incredibly, we have that famous French
tune to thank for director Bradley Cooper's

00:00:36.589 --> 00:00:41.090
A Star Is Born movie as we know it today because
not only did the song inspire the drag bar

00:00:41.090 --> 00:00:46.210
scene but also, crucially, it inspired Cooper
to cast Lady Gaga in the lead.

00:00:46.210 --> 00:00:50.780
Back in 2016, Cooper was still considering
who should play Ally when he was invited to

00:00:50.780 --> 00:00:55.250
a cancer benefit in LA where the superstar
singer happened to be performing.

00:00:55.250 --> 00:00:59.920
Cooper found himself so mesmerised by Gaga's
rendition of La Vie en Rose that he immediately

00:00:59.920 --> 00:01:03.470
decided to include the song and Gaga in his
movie.

00:01:03.470 --> 00:01:07.500
Straight after the event, Cooper got in touch
with her agent and set up a meeting at Gaga's

00:01:07.500 --> 00:01:10.910
Malibu home where he basically offered her
the role there and then.

00:01:10.910 --> 00:01:14.670
The two videoed themselves singing at the
piano together and reading scenes from the

00:01:14.670 --> 00:01:18.690
script, which convinced the studio that Cooper
had indeed found his perfect co-star.

00:01:18.690 --> 00:01:20.970
And the rest is A Star Is Born history!

00:01:20.970 --> 00:01:25.890
Oh, and it was Gaga's conversations with Cooper
about her early experiences in the music business

00:01:25.890 --> 00:01:29.500
and a particular drag bar where she used to
hang out that gave him the idea to create

00:01:29.500 --> 00:01:31.630
that scene.

00:01:31.630 --> 00:01:35.270
During the press tour for A Star Is Born,
Cooper and Gaga have talked often about the

00:01:35.270 --> 00:01:39.090
immediate connection they felt as soon as
they met and how they bonded over their East

00:01:39.090 --> 00:01:41.610
Coast Italian-American upbringing among other
things.

00:01:41.610 --> 00:01:46.020
And one particularly sweet moment during the
shoot shows just what close friends they became.

00:01:46.020 --> 00:01:50.380
After Cooper had filmed an especially tough
scene which was vital for his character, he

00:01:50.380 --> 00:01:54.850
walked up to Jackson's pick-up truck and opened
the door only to discover a bunch of roses

00:01:54.850 --> 00:01:57.790
that Gaga had left for him there on the passenger
seat.

00:01:57.790 --> 00:02:01.350
If you've seen the movie, you'll understand
why Cooper was so moved by Gaga's gesture

00:02:01.350 --> 00:02:05.960
as the scene he'd just filmed was a heart-breaking
one for Jackson.

00:02:05.960 --> 00:02:10.420
The soundtrack to A Star Is Born is jam-packed
with original songs, some of which were actually

00:02:10.420 --> 00:02:11.700
written during the shoot.

00:02:11.700 --> 00:02:16.240
For example, Lady Gaga wrote the song 'I Don't
Know What Love Is' when she felt completely

00:02:16.240 --> 00:02:19.610
overcome with emotion after filming the scene
in the cop bar.

00:02:19.610 --> 00:02:24.450
And she even used her character Ally's on-screen
notebook to write down the lyrics right there

00:02:24.450 --> 00:02:25.450
in the moment.

00:02:25.450 --> 00:02:29.620
She later finished off the song with Lukas
Nelson, son of country music star Willie Nelson.

00:02:29.620 --> 00:02:33.790
Lukas not only wrote and produced many of
the movie's original songs with Gaga and Cooper,

00:02:33.790 --> 00:02:37.970
but he and his bandmates from Promise of the
Real also doubled as Jackson Maine's band

00:02:37.970 --> 00:02:39.530
in the movie.

00:02:39.530 --> 00:02:44.500
Lady Gaga really hates watching movies where
you can tell the actors are lip-syncing, so,

00:02:44.500 --> 00:02:48.280
despite the fact that her co-star Bradley
Cooper had no real experience as a singer

00:02:48.280 --> 00:02:52.830
or musician before A Star Is Born, she convinced
him to record all their vocal performances

00:02:52.830 --> 00:02:57.580
live on the day of filming rather than simply
lip-syncing to pre-recorded tracks as often

00:02:57.580 --> 00:02:59.310
happens in movie musicals.

00:02:59.310 --> 00:03:03.599
Although first-time director Cooper found
singing live terrifying, he says it allowed

00:03:03.599 --> 00:03:06.940
him to capture 'the truth in each performance'.

00:03:06.940 --> 00:03:11.340
Many of the movie's musical moments were filmed
at real venues like Glastonbury Festival,

00:03:11.340 --> 00:03:15.270
so to avoid the crowd recording their brand
new songs and leaking them online ahead of

00:03:15.270 --> 00:03:19.330
the film's release, the sound crew deliberately
turned the amplifiers off so that the audience

00:03:19.330 --> 00:03:21.689
couldn't hear the music or vocals!

00:03:21.689 --> 00:03:25.970
That added another level of work for the movie's
sound team as they had to capture each venue's

00:03:25.970 --> 00:03:30.700
acoustics and apply them later in post-production
to make the voices sound as they would have

00:03:30.700 --> 00:03:32.860
done during a big concert!

00:03:32.860 --> 00:03:36.840
Using such enormous real-life performance
spaces like LA's Greek Theatre and the Shrine

00:03:36.840 --> 00:03:40.760
Auditorium meant the production needed lots
of people in the audience to get the right

00:03:40.760 --> 00:03:44.780
visuals, energy, and enthusiasm to make the
concerts look and feel real!

00:03:44.780 --> 00:03:49.620
But instead of using thousands of extras,
the filmmakers instead turned to Lady Gaga's

00:03:49.620 --> 00:03:53.599
dedicated fan base, known as her Little Monsters,
who were given the chance to buy tickets for

00:03:53.599 --> 00:03:57.610
each of the venues where filming took place,
all the proceeds from which went to Gaga's

00:03:57.610 --> 00:03:59.520
Born This Way Foundation.

00:03:59.520 --> 00:04:03.350
And as an extra thank-you to her fans at the
end of a late night filming, Gaga gave an

00:04:03.350 --> 00:04:06.659
impromptu piano performance of two of her
hits.

00:04:06.659 --> 00:04:11.070
Bradley Cooper may have many years' experience
acting on camera, but when it came to playing

00:04:11.070 --> 00:04:15.800
a seasoned singer and musician and performing
live on stage, he realised he needed to dedicate

00:04:15.800 --> 00:04:19.019
plenty of time to preparing for the musical
aspects of the part.

00:04:19.019 --> 00:04:23.550
So, he got himself a vocal coach and spent
five days a week for six months learning how

00:04:23.550 --> 00:04:27.379
to sing not just as himself, but also in character
as Jackson Maine.

00:04:27.379 --> 00:04:31.159
To give you an idea of the kind of progress
Cooper made with his singing, when he first

00:04:31.159 --> 00:04:34.370
started, he found himself getting out of breath
after just one verse.

00:04:34.370 --> 00:04:38.979
So, he certainly came a long way from that
to performing so many songs live on film.

00:04:38.979 --> 00:04:43.300
Cooper also took guitar and piano lessons
and worked pretty much every night for twelve

00:04:43.300 --> 00:04:47.539
months with Lukas Nelson who also shared his
own insights on performing and acting like

00:04:47.539 --> 00:04:49.169
a professional musician.

00:04:49.169 --> 00:04:54.139
But Cooper didn't just work on his singing
voice; he also spent months working on his

00:04:54.139 --> 00:04:58.889
speaking voice, using a dialect coach to help
him develop the rich timbre he wanted for

00:04:58.889 --> 00:05:00.300
Jackson Maine's voice.

00:05:00.300 --> 00:05:04.830
It proved to be a real challenge and initially
it was even painful, but Cooper felt that

00:05:04.830 --> 00:05:09.219
lowering his own range by about an octave
would give his character the kind of presence

00:05:09.219 --> 00:05:13.879
iconic musicians have and cinema audiences
would feel that as soon as they saw Jackson

00:05:13.879 --> 00:05:15.020
on screen.

00:05:15.020 --> 00:05:18.919
Cooper dropped his own voice to more or less
match the register of actor Sam Elliott, who

00:05:18.919 --> 00:05:20.080
plays his on-screen brother.

00:05:20.080 --> 00:05:24.300
And, apparently, all that time Cooper spent
listening to interviews with Elliott to hone

00:05:24.300 --> 00:05:28.569
his new voice paid off because when he played
a recording of himself during his first meeting

00:05:28.569 --> 00:05:32.729
with Elliott, the veteran actor was amazed
at how much Cooper's voice sounded like his

00:05:32.729 --> 00:05:33.729
own!

00:05:33.729 --> 00:05:38.559
Although Gaga already has a Golden Globe for
American Horror Story, A Star Is Born is her

00:05:38.559 --> 00:05:42.229
first lead role on the big screen, and it
took a little while for her to feel at home

00:05:42.229 --> 00:05:43.229
on set.

00:05:43.229 --> 00:05:46.900
While she knew all her lines on her first
day of filming, she was so thrown when Bradley

00:05:46.900 --> 00:05:50.479
Cooper went off-script for a moment in an
effort to help her relax and 'let go of the

00:05:50.479 --> 00:05:55.099
words', that she just kept repeating her same
line again and again, before bursting into

00:05:55.099 --> 00:05:56.099
tears!

00:05:56.099 --> 00:05:59.910
Gaga and Cooper soon created a shorthand between
themselves though to get the right mood for

00:05:59.910 --> 00:06:00.910
each scene.

00:06:00.910 --> 00:06:04.919
For example, to conjure up a certain warmth
in her performance, Cooper would say the name

00:06:04.919 --> 00:06:09.909
'Tony', to remind Gaga of her great friend
and singer Tony Bennett, who she adores.

00:06:09.909 --> 00:06:14.840
But if Gaga had to really concentrate, then
Cooper would say 'ninja' or 'assassin'.

00:06:14.840 --> 00:06:19.099
Just before Lady Gaga was due to film a really
big, emotional scene on stage at the Shrine

00:06:19.099 --> 00:06:24.110
Auditorium, she got a devastating phone call
that her best friend Sonja was dying of cancer.

00:06:24.110 --> 00:06:28.309
So, she jumped in her car and drove straight
to Sonja's side, though she sadly missed her

00:06:28.309 --> 00:06:30.770
friend's passing by just moments.

00:06:30.770 --> 00:06:34.930
When Gaga later returned to set, she took
to the stage and gave a heart-wrenching performance

00:06:34.930 --> 00:06:38.969
of "I'll Never Love Again", an especially
moving song for her character Ally in a scene

00:06:38.969 --> 00:06:40.699
that Gaga says she'll never forget.

00:06:40.699 --> 00:06:43.910
So, have you seen the new A Star Is Born movie?

00:06:43.910 --> 00:06:45.399
And what did you think of it?

